# tool/transient_py/.gitignore — namespace-local policy
#
# Spec: docs/anima_dot_own_namespace_spec_2026_05_03.md
# Rationale: This namespace holds .own 2 (auto-gen transpiler output) and
# .own 4 (test fixtures) .py files that MUST be regeneratable from the
# parent .hexa SSOT. Tracking would create dual SSOT (raw 0 violation).
#
# What is tracked here:
#   .gitkeep   — preserve empty directory in git
#   .gitignore — this file (per-namespace policy)
#   README.md  — human-readable namespace explanation
#
# What is gitignored:
#   *.py            — all auto-generated python (.own 2 / .own 4)
#   __pycache__/    — bytecode cache
#   *.pyc           — compiled bytecode
#
# Note: this ignore is REDUNDANT with the root `**/*.py` ban in /.gitignore
# but is kept here as namespace-local documentation (raw 91 honest C5 —
# explicit-over-implicit when a sub-namespace has policy semantics).

*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Negate tracked metadata files (allow them through git add)
!.gitkeep
!.gitignore
!README.md
